# Copy to deploy/docker/.env. Every value has a default.

# The directory holding this deployment's secrets, mounted read-only at
# /run/athanor. It must contain the key policy, and the vault key when the
# live-database path is used.
#
# It has to be READABLE BY UID 10001. The image runs as an unprivileged user
# of its own and a key file locked down to the account that wrote it — which
# is the right thing to do with a key file — is a file the container cannot
# open, and what a reader sees is a container restarting with "permission
# denied" every two seconds:
#
#   chown -R 10001:10001 /path/to/secrets && chmod 700 /path/to/secrets
#
ATHANOR_SECRETS=.
ATHANOR_KEYS_NAME=keys.json

ATHANOR_GRPC_PORT=47831
ATHANOR_HTTP_PORT=47832
ATHANOR_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Health probe needs a key when a key file is in force; give it a read-only one.
ATHANOR_TOKEN=

# Where AdminService.Backup may write. Inside the container, so on the volume.
#ATHANOR_BACKUP_DIR=/data/backups

# The live-database path.
#
# A plan that pseudonymizes anything cannot be signed without a vault, and the
# classifier reaches for pseudonymize on a name column by default — so a
# deployment meant to read a live database wants all three of these, and the
# key is 32 raw bytes or 64 hex characters (`openssl rand -hex 32`) in a file
# inside ATHANOR_SECRETS.
#ATHANOR_VAULT=/data/vault.db
#ATHANOR_VAULT_KEY=/run/athanor/vault.key
#ATHANOR_VAULT_TENANT=
# Hosts a plan may name, comma-separated. Empty is every host.
#ATHANOR_LIVEDB_HOSTS=

# Optional embedder for the brain's recall. Unset is lexical mode.
#OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
#OPENAI_API_KEY=local
#CORTEXDB_EMBED_MODEL=embeddinggemma
#CORTEXDB_EMBED_DIM=768
